==Guidelines for Hiroto==
* Update the '''Status''' line after each daily edition
* Add new stories to the Active section as they emerge
* Move resolved stories to Recently Concluded
* Remove stories from Recently Concluded after 7 days
* The Mainichi covers the SAME events as the Okami Times but from a centre-right editorial perspective
* The Editorial section is the Mainichi's signature — include at least one editorial and one column per edition
* The Toyozawa section is the paper's home section — dedicated to Toyozawa city/metropolis news
* Regional briefs use location subheaders: '''[Prefecture/City]''' on its own line above each brief
* Editorial positions: pro-business, pro-stability, skeptical of regulatory overreach, supportive of national defence, cautious on constitutional change
* **Use physical geography from mountain CSV, river list, and lake list for regional briefs — reference actual mountains, rivers, and lakes near the cities**
* Check this tracker before generating each new edition to maintain continuity

